SIDE-LOCKED (hang), NOT MEASURED on ['vg8020', 'cf3300', 'zb']: ['kwgz-auto', 'kwgz-ctl', 'kwgz-delete', 'kwgz-llist', 'kwgz-renum'] -- AUTO enters interactive line-entry and LLIST drives an unplugged LPTOUT; both HANG a reference machine (the keyword sweep already files them as crunch-only for this reason). They are measurable only on ['zb'], and they gate nothing.

CAPABILITY-LOCKED dsk-ctl: measured on ['cf3300', 'zb'] only -- the VG-8020 has no disk interface, so `A:` is not a device there; the row gates cf3300 against zerobas.
CAPABILITY-LOCKED dsk-load: measured on ['cf3300', 'zb'] only -- the VG-8020 has no disk interface, so `A:` is not a device there; the row gates cf3300 against zerobas.
CAPABILITY-LOCKED dsk-mrg: measured on ['cf3300', 'zb'] only -- the VG-8020 has no disk interface, so `A:` is not a device there; the row gates cf3300 against zerobas.
CAPABILITY-LOCKED dsk-savasc: measured on ['cf3300', 'zb'] only -- the VG-8020 has no disk interface, so `A:` is not a device there; the row gates cf3300 against zerobas.
CAPABILITY-LOCKED dsk-savtok: measured on ['cf3300', 'zb'] only -- the VG-8020 has no disk interface, so `A:` is not a device there; the row gates cf3300 against zerobas.

SELF-HEAL: re-running 2 suspect row(s) boot-per-case -- a batched mangle reads exactly like a divergence, and --repeat cannot tell them apart.
  ⚠️ GATING rows needing the heal (a batched mangle, or a real divergence -- read the healed value below):
      crf-oomsay    batched: vg8020=Out of memory | cf3300=Out of memory | zb=<nothing listed>
      crf-oomlst    batched: vg8020=99 REM Z | cf3300=99 REM Z | zb=20 REM BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB|99 REM Z

